176.0, 492.0], [1344.0, 493.0], [1344.0, 529.0], [176.0, 528.0]], 'NRN site and gestational age (< 26 °/7 weeks vs. ≥ 26 °/7 weeks), noting that an NRN center may', 0.9895298537455107], [[[178.0, 529.0], [1315.0, 529.0], [1315.0, 562.0], [178.0, 562.0]], 'have more than one site (hospital/NICU). Infants who are randomized to the < 26 °/7 strata but', 0.9869767776195039], [[[181.0, 565.0], [1276.0, 565.0], [1276.0, 595.0], [181.0, 595.0]], 'advance to the next GA strata prior to the first dose will still be classified as their originally', 0.9766435665743691], [[[180.0, 600.0], [1335.0, 598.0], [1335.0, 628.0], [180.0, 630.0]], 'assigned strata for the purpose of this analysis. Infants who are randomized to the ≥ 26 °/7 strata', 0.9909058327626701], [[[178.0, 633.0], [1347.0, 635.0], [1347.0, 665.0], [178.0, 663.0]], 'but advance to 29 °/7 weeks GA prior to their first dose (and have a birth weight > 1000g) remain', 0.9793646679711097], [[[177.0, 667.0], [1328.0, 668.0], [1328.0, 701.0], [177.0, 700.0]], 'in the intention-to-treat (ITT) population, but should not receive treatment as they are no longer', 0.9986680928541689], [[[182.0, 701.0], [437.0, 705.0], [437.0, 738.0], [181.0, 734.0]], 'eligible for the study.', 0.9988903118216473], [[[181.0, 765.0], [1292.0, 766.0], [1292.0, 799.0], [181.0, 798.0]], 'All randomization will be performed by the Data Coordinating Center (DCC) at RTI, via the', 0.9981215823902173], [[[181.0, 802.0], [1336.0, 802.0], [1336.0, 833.0], [181.0, 833.0]], 'block urn design with a stratum-specific maximum tolerable imbalance known only to the DCC.', 0.9935947211234124], [[[180.0, 836.0], [1270.0, 836.0], [1270.0, 869.0], [180.0, 869.0]], 'The block urn design was proposed by Zhao and Weng (2011) as a modification of the urn', 0.9871318270993787], [[[181.0, 872.0], [1304.0, 872.0], [1304.0, 902.0], [181.0, 902.0]], 'design and alternative to the permuted block design in order to maintain consistent imbalance', 0.9914466655382546], [[[180.0, 905.0], [1326.0, 907.0], [1326.0, 936.0], [180.0, 934.0]], 'control under the maximum tolerable imbalance between treatment groups, while also lowering', 0.9891120090589418], [[[180.0, 940.0], [1296.0, 940.0], [1296.0, 973.0], [180.0, 973.0]], 'the probabilities of deterministic assignments. By having lower probabilities of deterministic', 0.9886339883855049], [[[179.0, 975.0], [1251.0, 974.0], [1251.0, 1004.0], [179.0, 1005.0]], 'assignments than the stratified permuted block design, the block urn design decreases the', 0.9873084988486901], [[[178.0, 1009.0], [1302.0, 1009.0], [1302.0, 1042.0], [178.0, 1042.0]], 'probability of correct guessing, and thus inadvertent unmasking of research staff and possible', 0.990596168218775], [[[179.0, 1042.0], [354.0, 1044.0], [353.0, 1074.0], [178.0, 1072.0]], 'selection bias.', 0.9995440125465394], [[[179.0, 1108.0], [1307.0, 1109.0], [1307.0, 1139.0], [179.0, 1138.0]], 'As an overview,  balls of one color and  balls of another color are placed into an active urn,', 0.9829895134935988], [[[180.0, 1142.0], [1328.0, 1145.0], [1328.0, 1175.0], [180.0, 1172.0]], 'where A is the maximum tolerable imbalance between the arms and each color corresponds to a', 0.9799636209404076], [[[178.0, 1178.0], [1343.0, 1179.0], [1343.0, 1209.0], [178.0, 1208.0]], 'treatment arm. As a color-coded ball is selected (representing randomization to a treatment arm),', 0.9857681571822805], [[[180.0, 1213.0], [1312.0, 1213.0], [1312.0, 1241.0], [180.0, 1241.0]], 'the ball is placed into an inactive urn. Once there is a set of two balls, one of each color, in the', 0.977605277299881], [[[180.0, 1247.0], [1246.0, 1247.0], [1246.0, 1276.0], [180.0, 1276.0]], 'inactive urn, these balls are returned to the active urn and are available for selection. The', 0.986622638920302], [[[177.0, 1281.0], [1264.0, 1283.0], [1264.0, 1316.0], [177.0, 1314.0]], 'probability of assignment to the intervention arm for the i-th subject is represented by PiA,', 0.9864132788873488], [[[601.0, 1344.0], [1008.0, 1350.0], [1008.0, 1387.0], [600.0, 1381.0]], 'A + min(Ni-1,A, Ni-1,c) - Ni-1,A', 0.9147449936717749], [[[504.0, 1371.0], [579.0, 1380.0], [575.0, 1413.0], [500.0, 1404.0]], 'PiA =', 0.9504832744598388], [[[578.0, 1391.0], [1028.0, 1393.0], [1028.0, 1433.0], [578.0, 1431.0]], '2入 + 2min(Ni-1,A, Ni-1,c) - (i - 1)', 0.9334467270544597], [[[181.0, 1463.0], [1348.0, 1465.0], [1348.0, 1495.0], [181.0, 1493.0]], 'where Nia is the number of infants allocated to the intervention arm among the i subjects and Nic', 0.9891570511552477], [[[177.0, 1497.0], [1352.0, 1498.0], [1352.0, 1531.0], [177.0, 1530.0]], 'is the number of infants allocated to the control arm among the i subjects. Thus, determination of', 0.9924433955124446], [[[179.0, 1534.0], [1338.0, 1534.0], [1338.0, 1566.0], [179.0, 1566.0]], 'the probabilities of treatment assignment take a closed form and are straightforward to calculate.', 0.9824849719903908], [[[178.0, 1567.0], [1294.0, 1570.0], [1294.0, 1600.0], [178.0, 1597.0]], 'Randomization schedules will be generated via the block urn design and supplied to the sites', 0.9955502379199733], [[[179.0, 1605.0], [578.0, 1604.0], [578.0, 1634.0], [179.0, 1635.0]], 'prior to commencing enrollment.', 0.9929077856002315], [[[179.0, 1667.0], [623.0, 1670.0], [622.0, 1700.0], [179.0, 1697.0]], '4.4General Masking Procedures', 0.9832652889449021], [[[180.0, 1731.0], [1273.0, 1733.0], [1273.0, 1762.0], [180.0, 1761.0]], 'This study will be masked, and all attempts will be made to maintain masking to the extent', 0.9893433849016825], [[[180.0, 1767.0], [1335.0, 1767.0], [1335.0, 1798.0], [180.0, 1798.0]], 'possible. Select DCC personnel will be unmasked to treatment allocation, while the senior study', 0.9956799055400648], [[[180.0, 1835.0], [379.0, 1838.0], [378.0, 1864.0], [179.0, 1861.0]], 'Version 1.3,2024-09-10', 0.9890117672356692], [[[1284.0, 1836.0], [1353.0, 1836.0], [1353.0, 1864.0], [1284.0, 1864.0]], 'Page 10', 0.99600967339106